# S0: status of the four-card set, an all-four reset with the heal (so the one-card jobs after it start from freshly trained boards,
# and a card, link or hugepage fault fails here, before an hour of card M), then build the tp4-s2 image. Run first: it is the
# cheapest job and the only one every later quad job depends on.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); build 7-15 min when the image's layers are cached (the bundle stage is; only the
# overlay and the profiles are new), 30-70 min cold (step limit 75). It runs the image copy-closure and overlay tests inside the
# P8 base first, then G1 provenance, and tags the image only if they pass, so a closure error fails here with no card touched.
# Read: the status listing (four boards by id, one firmware bundle on all of them, at least four free 1 GiB hugepages, no
# holders, NO platform serving container, disk for a new ~32 GB image), then the build log (closure tests OK, provenance passed).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
